WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.090 --> 00:00:05.770
The Pet Sematary remake unleashes a new twist
on the supernatural horrors of Stephen King's

00:00:05.770 --> 00:00:07.070
spine-chilling novel.

00:00:07.070 --> 00:00:11.320
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, I'm Jan and in
this video I'm breaking down everything you

00:00:11.320 --> 00:00:15.620
need to know about the shocking ending to
the new Pet Sematary, including the true nature

00:00:15.620 --> 00:00:19.560
of the demonic force in the movie and the
crucial changes from the original story.

00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:24.080
Plus, keep watching to the end for some bonus
Stephen King easter eggs you might have missed.

00:00:24.080 --> 00:00:27.539
Spoilers ahead so take care if you haven't
seen the movie yet.

00:00:27.539 --> 00:00:31.240
The real antagonist at the heart of the Pet
Sematary story is the Wendigo demon.

00:00:31.240 --> 00:00:36.120
After Jud and Louis find Ellie's beloved cat
Church dead by the side of the road, they

00:00:36.120 --> 00:00:38.120
take it to the Pet Sematary for burial.

00:00:38.120 --> 00:00:43.320
As they go to bury the dead pet, Jud feels
the pull of the Wendigo's spirit, so instead

00:00:43.320 --> 00:00:48.489
he leads Louis over a barrier of sticks, through
the woods and a swamp to an ancient Micmac

00:00:48.489 --> 00:00:49.489
burial ground.

00:00:49.489 --> 00:00:54.899
Jud then tells Louis to bury Church in this
creepy place that's full of whispering voices.

00:00:54.899 --> 00:00:59.840
A reanimated Church then appears at the family
house the next day though he's much dirtier

00:00:59.840 --> 00:01:01.180
and meaner.

00:01:01.180 --> 00:01:04.470
Confused, Louis visits Jud to demand an explanation.

00:01:04.470 --> 00:01:08.819
Jud tells him about the stories he's heard
about the Wendigo, a malevolent demon feared

00:01:08.819 --> 00:01:12.939
by native American tribes in the northern
regions of the US and Canada.

00:01:12.939 --> 00:01:16.840
The signs carved into the trees in the woods
on the way to the burial ground, which Louis

00:01:16.840 --> 00:01:21.170
also sees in the book at Jud's house, are
warnings left by the Micmac people before

00:01:21.170 --> 00:01:22.659
they fled the area.

00:01:22.659 --> 00:01:27.689
They also built a deadfall as a wall or barrier
to stop people going into the cursed area.

00:01:27.689 --> 00:01:31.970
The ground beyond that barrier was soured
or cursed by the Wendigo, meaning that if

00:01:31.970 --> 00:01:36.450
a person or animal is buried in the old Micmac
graveyard, they are reanimated and end up

00:01:36.450 --> 00:01:38.990
possessed by the spirit of the evil demon.

00:01:38.990 --> 00:01:43.590
For example, even after Louis realises the
danger the resurrected Church poses to his

00:01:43.590 --> 00:01:48.149
family and takes the possessed cat far away,
the power of the Wendigo inside Church is

00:01:48.149 --> 00:01:52.869
too strong and the cat makes his way back
to the family home deliberately luring Ellie

00:01:52.869 --> 00:01:57.170
into the road in front of a speeding truck,
and jumping out of the way to safety just

00:01:57.170 --> 00:01:59.270
before it crashes into her.

00:01:59.270 --> 00:02:01.789
The change in Ellie is even more noticeable.

00:02:01.789 --> 00:02:06.570
Initially after she returns from the dead,
she's unsure where she is but quickly understands

00:02:06.570 --> 00:02:10.119
that she's changed and she says to Louis "I'm
dead, aren't I?"

00:02:10.119 --> 00:02:15.120
She also tells him she can hear the woods
inside her, another indication that the Wendigo's

00:02:15.120 --> 00:02:17.939
spirit has invaded and occupied her body.

00:02:17.939 --> 00:02:22.000
The demon also gives her an unnatural physical
strength that a nine-year-old girl would be

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:26.260
unlikely to possess such as being able to
drag her mother's body all the way to the

00:02:26.260 --> 00:02:31.010
burial ground by herself and, when she fights
her father, he finds it extremely difficult

00:02:31.010 --> 00:02:32.510
to overpower her.

00:02:32.510 --> 00:02:37.140
On top of that, the Wendigo can manipulate
Ellie's body to communicate and taunt the

00:02:37.140 --> 00:02:38.629
victims she's about to kill.

00:02:38.629 --> 00:02:43.500
When she attacks Jud, Ellie tells him how
she saw his dead wife Norma burning in hell,

00:02:43.500 --> 00:02:48.400
and then the Wendigo even transforms Ellie's
body and voice momentarily into Norma.

00:02:48.400 --> 00:02:50.900
The possessed Ellie does the same with her
mother, Rachel.

00:02:50.900 --> 00:02:55.019
First she blames her mother for leaving her
to die in the road and then accuses her of

00:02:55.019 --> 00:02:57.689
having done the same with her sister Zelda.

00:02:57.689 --> 00:03:02.260
Like Jud who refuses to believe he's seeing
the real Norma, Rachel tells Ellie "you're

00:03:02.260 --> 00:03:06.879
not my daughter", to which the now possessed
Ellie replies "then go be with her", at which

00:03:06.879 --> 00:03:09.180
point she stabs Rachel once more.

00:03:09.180 --> 00:03:13.640
There's an interesting similarity between
how the Wendigo exerts an evil influence on

00:03:13.640 --> 00:03:19.230
people in Pet Sematary and how Pennywise influences
people to commit terrible deeds in IT.

00:03:19.230 --> 00:03:23.280
On top of that, there's a deliberate easter
egg to Stephen King's IT with a road sign

00:03:23.280 --> 00:03:27.189
for Derry in the scene where Rachel and Gage
are stuck in a traffic jam as they try to

00:03:27.189 --> 00:03:28.819
get back to Ludlow.

00:03:28.819 --> 00:03:33.280
Derry is, of course, the town in Maine where
IT takes place and where Pennywise shows up

00:03:33.280 --> 00:03:35.340
every 27 years.

00:03:35.340 --> 00:03:39.469
In contrast to IT though, where the Losers'
Club is able to band together to defeat the

00:03:39.469 --> 00:03:42.870
evil spirit, Pet Sematary has a much, much
darker ending.

00:03:42.870 --> 00:03:48.700
In fact, the 2019 remake goes further perhaps
than the 1989 movie or the original novel

00:03:48.700 --> 00:03:52.480
in terms of how many of the Creed family are
killed by the Wendigo.

00:03:52.480 --> 00:03:56.670
In this version, Ellie is first killed by
the truck; Ellie then kills her mother and

00:03:56.670 --> 00:04:01.069
resurrects her; and then as Louis fights with
Ellie, the reanimated Rachel comes out of

00:04:01.069 --> 00:04:04.569
nowhere and mortally spears Louis through
the back.

00:04:04.569 --> 00:04:08.900
After they drag his body off to the Micmac
burial ground, we cut to a chilling final

00:04:08.900 --> 00:04:13.120
scene of Gage helplessly waiting in the family
car outside their home.

00:04:13.120 --> 00:04:19.090
Louis, Ellie and Rachel then appear walking
towards the car, Church jumps menacingly into

00:04:19.090 --> 00:04:24.620
view, and as the screen cuts to black there's
the horrifying sound of the car doors unlocking.

00:04:24.620 --> 00:04:28.910
If you have any doubt about whether Gage survived,
there's actually a clue in the opening scene

00:04:28.910 --> 00:04:31.259
of the movie which heavily implies that he
didn't.

00:04:31.259 --> 00:04:34.780
The scene shows the aftermath after the car
door was unlocked.

00:04:34.780 --> 00:04:38.620
The door has been opened and there are a couple
of bloody handprints on the window plus some

00:04:38.620 --> 00:04:40.470
blood inside the door.

00:04:40.470 --> 00:04:44.370
It seems pretty likely then that the possessed
bodies of the Creed family will have killed

00:04:44.370 --> 00:04:49.139
Gage and dragged him off to bury and resurrect
him, providing the evil Wendigo demon with

00:04:49.139 --> 00:04:51.009
yet another corpse to inhabit.

00:04:51.009 --> 00:04:54.660
However, in the original story, it's just
Gage and Rachel who are killed.

00:04:54.660 --> 00:05:00.650
They're both buried by Louis and resurrected,
and in the 1989 movie Rachel also kills Louis

00:05:00.650 --> 00:05:01.919
after she returns.

00:05:01.919 --> 00:05:06.250
There's also a couple of other major characters
we need to talk about.

00:05:06.250 --> 00:05:10.320
First of all is Zelda, Rachel's sister, who
has a terrifying part to play in the remake

00:05:10.320 --> 00:05:13.629
and gets more screentime than in the 1989
movie.

00:05:13.629 --> 00:05:17.729
We learn in the film that Zelda suffered from
spinal meningitis and there's a particularly

00:05:17.729 --> 00:05:21.990
scary scene where we see just how badly she
traumatised Rachel.

00:05:21.990 --> 00:05:26.110
Rachel who was left alone by her parents to
care for her sick sister used a dumbwaiter

00:05:26.110 --> 00:05:31.370
to send food up to Zelda, but after the food
got stuck, Zelda died in a horrific mangled

00:05:31.370 --> 00:05:33.979
mess when she fell into the dumbwaiter.

00:05:33.979 --> 00:05:38.419
And after Rachel and her family move to Ludlow,
it feels like the spirit of the Wendigo that

00:05:38.419 --> 00:05:42.849
stalks the land surrounding their new house
plays a part in summoning the terrible recurring

00:05:42.849 --> 00:05:45.550
visions of Zelda that Rachel begins to suffer.

00:05:45.550 --> 00:05:50.530
After the resurrected Church returns to the
house and starts acting maliciously, for example,

00:05:50.530 --> 00:05:55.240
by scratching Ellie for the first time, not
only does Louis hear a terrible groaning sound

00:05:55.240 --> 00:05:59.310
from the basement with a warning that "the
destruction of all he loves is very near",

00:05:59.310 --> 00:06:03.539
but Rachel starts to hear terrible thumping
noises from the roof and inside the walls

00:06:03.539 --> 00:06:08.090
which culminate in a petrifying vision of
her dead sister appearing inside the bathroom

00:06:08.090 --> 00:06:13.060
cabinet in a similar way to how Zelda died
inside the Dumbwaiter years ago.

00:06:13.060 --> 00:06:17.210
Rachel's case shows us again how the Wendigo
is able to use the grief, shame and sense

00:06:17.210 --> 00:06:22.199
of regret someone may suffer after a terrible
tragedy to manipulate its victims psychologically

00:06:22.199 --> 00:06:24.550
and eventually cause their downfall.

00:06:24.550 --> 00:06:29.699
We also need to talk about Victor Pascow who
plays a small but important part as a voice

00:06:29.699 --> 00:06:33.699
who repeatedly warns Louis against the dangers
of crossing the deadfall.

00:06:33.699 --> 00:06:37.870
He also tries to warn Louis against taking
the dead Ellie up to the burial ground, though

00:06:37.870 --> 00:06:39.750
of course Louis ignores him.

00:06:39.750 --> 00:06:43.100
And Pascow also warns Gage and Rachel that
Louis is in danger.

00:06:43.100 --> 00:06:48.199
Now, some people have theorised that Pascow
may not be acting so benevolently in Pet Sematary

00:06:48.199 --> 00:06:52.520
because you could argue that he not only draws
Louis's attention to the deadfall, but he

00:06:52.520 --> 00:06:56.939
also leads Rachel and Gage back to Ludlow
placing them in danger so that they eventually

00:06:56.939 --> 00:06:58.759
become possessed by the Wendigo.

00:06:58.759 --> 00:07:03.770
However, if we take Pascow at face value as
a caution and remember that it was Jud who

00:07:03.770 --> 00:07:07.940
took Louis over the threshold, I think that
Pascow is a character that serves to draw

00:07:07.940 --> 00:07:12.020
our attention to the folly of ignoring the
warnings in front us.

00:07:12.020 --> 00:07:16.000
Pet Sematary also warns us of the dangers
of not learning how to deal with grief and

00:07:16.000 --> 00:07:17.380
tragedy appropriately.

00:07:17.380 --> 00:07:22.080
For instance, after Louis discovers Church
has died, Rachel, who's never been able to

00:07:22.080 --> 00:07:27.189
get over the death of her sister, asks Louis
to tell Ellie that her cat ran way.

00:07:27.189 --> 00:07:30.849
Basically, Rachel asks him to say anything
except that the cat died.

00:07:30.849 --> 00:07:36.330
Likewise, after Ellie dies, Louis can't accept
her death or his feelings of guilt and regret

00:07:36.330 --> 00:07:40.720
at insisting on staying in Ludlow after both
Ellie and Rachel asked to move back to Boston.

00:07:40.720 --> 00:07:45.440
So, he deliberately makes an excuse to stay
behind when Rachel and Gage go to stay with

00:07:45.440 --> 00:07:50.020
her family, and he also drugs Jud so he doesn't
stop him from digging up the dead Ellie and

00:07:50.020 --> 00:07:51.620
taking her to be resurrected.

00:07:51.620 --> 00:07:56.490
Jud, who also didn't want to see Ellie sad
at the loss of Church, was the original instigator,

00:07:56.490 --> 00:07:59.650
of course, in taking the dead cat to be resurrected.

00:07:59.650 --> 00:08:04.319
All of these terrible decisions show the folly
of not facing up to reality and instead turning

00:08:04.319 --> 00:08:08.840
to superstition or toying with supernatural
forces we don't understand.

00:08:08.840 --> 00:08:12.431
I've already touched on a few Pet Sematary
book and movie easter eggs, but there's some

00:08:12.431 --> 00:08:14.490
other interesting ones you might have missed.

00:08:14.490 --> 00:08:19.270
Ellie refers to herself as Ellie the Great
and Terrible both before she becomes possessed

00:08:19.270 --> 00:08:20.639
and afterwards.

00:08:20.639 --> 00:08:24.621
The nickname isn't just a neat little bit
of foreshadowing of her terrible fate, it's

00:08:24.621 --> 00:08:29.520
also an easter egg to book Zelda who had a
picture on her wall of Oz the Great and Terrible

00:08:29.520 --> 00:08:31.370
that smashed when she died.

00:08:31.370 --> 00:08:35.850
In King's novel, Oz the Great and Terrible
becomes a theme associated with an unnatural

00:08:35.850 --> 00:08:40.610
and evil death and so, of course, it's especially
fitting that it's a title that Ellie assumes

00:08:40.610 --> 00:08:43.980
before she's taken over by the wicked Wendigo
spirit.

00:08:43.980 --> 00:08:47.890
An easter egg that flashes by pretty quickly
is when the truck driver who accidentally

00:08:47.890 --> 00:08:52.050
kills Ellie gets distracted by a phone call
from Sheena just before the accident.

00:08:52.050 --> 00:08:56.900
"Sheena Is A Punk Rocker" is the song by the
Ramones that the truck driver from the 1989

00:08:56.900 --> 00:09:01.080
movie was playing in his vehicle during the
accident that killed Gage.

00:09:01.080 --> 00:09:04.920
In fact, the decision by the filmmakers of
this remake to change the child killed in

00:09:04.920 --> 00:09:09.880
the accident did upset some King purists who
prefer the idea of the youngest child becoming

00:09:09.880 --> 00:09:13.340
corrupted by the Wendigo and being turned
into a murderous infant.

00:09:13.340 --> 00:09:17.390
For this movie though, I think it turned out
to be great change and twist.

00:09:17.390 --> 00:09:21.630
Jeté Laurence who plays Ellie in the new
movie delivered a fantastic performance as

00:09:21.630 --> 00:09:26.140
both the sweet-natured Ellie before her death
and the angry murderously possessed Ellie

00:09:26.140 --> 00:09:27.940
after her resurrection.

00:09:27.940 --> 00:09:31.580
Having the older child come back from the
dead also allowed her to interact with her

00:09:31.580 --> 00:09:35.680
family in a way that just wouldn't have been
possible or realistic with a toddler.

00:09:35.680 --> 00:09:39.630
And if you're wondering whether there's likely
to be a sequel that follows on from these

00:09:39.630 --> 00:09:44.100
events, well, the directors have said they're
much more interested in a possible prequel

00:09:44.100 --> 00:09:45.100
story.

00:09:45.100 --> 00:09:48.830
In an interview with Consequence of Sound,
producer Lorenzo di Bonaventura said that

00:09:48.830 --> 00:09:50.740
"if there's anything here, there's a prequel.

00:09:50.740 --> 00:09:54.540
[…] If you look at the book, we didn't cover
all that stuff that happens before the Creed

00:09:54.540 --> 00:09:55.540
family moves in."

00:09:55.540 --> 00:09:59.360
As he says, there are stories from King's
original book which weren't included in this

00:09:59.360 --> 00:10:04.180
adaptation but which were included in the
1989 movie, such as how one of the town's

00:10:04.180 --> 00:10:09.320
deceased World War 2 veterans, Timmy Baterman,
was resurrected after his body was sent back

00:10:09.320 --> 00:10:11.110
to the town from the war.

00:10:11.110 --> 00:10:15.380
There was a tiny easter egg to this in the
new movie via a newspaper headline that flashes

00:10:15.380 --> 00:10:17.200
by very quickly.

00:10:17.200 --> 00:10:21.310
Another area that could be explored in a prequel
is a jump further back in time to when the

00:10:21.310 --> 00:10:24.550
native Americans were still in the area around
Ludlow.

00:10:24.550 --> 00:10:28.710
This remake deliberately pointed out that
the entire plot of land that the Creeds owned

00:10:28.710 --> 00:10:32.010
extended back to the Pet Sematary and beyond
the barrier.

00:10:32.010 --> 00:10:36.240
And when Louis was reading about the Wendigo
in Jud's house, there was a newspaper headline

00:10:36.240 --> 00:10:39.090
that read "Indian land claims still unsettled".

00:10:39.090 --> 00:10:43.750
A prequel could investigate what part the
Wendigo might have played in any conflict

00:10:43.750 --> 00:10:47.720
over land between native American tribes and
those who settled the town of Ludlow.

00:10:47.720 --> 00:10:51.050
Now, if you've seen both movies, which did
you prefer?

